From d2de04944d1404cc57bc5b0ab7017aacf5ebef28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:09:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 109/114] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350: describe CPU capacity and
 power

Every core reported a capacity of 1024, so the scheduler treated the A55s, A78s
and X1 as equals and ran browser work on small cores by chance. Add the vendor
tree's capacity and power coefficient values, which sc7280 also uses upstream.

Capacities are now 325, 828 and 1024. In a Firefox scrolling test, stalls over
100 ms dropped from 1-10 per 30 s to 0-1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
index 2b5a0b8c0fe..16ed4f7ea50 100644
